# Copy to .privacy-denylist (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# One term per line. Case-insensitive substring match against every published
# file — skills/**, site/src/content/**, site/src/pages/**, commands/**, root *.md.
# `#` starts a comment. Terms shorter than 2 characters are ignored.
#
# What belongs here: the names structure alone cannot catch — customer and
# employer organisations, internal programme codenames, private drive or team
# names. The structural rules in scripts/check_publish_privacy.py already cover
# operator paths, drive mounts, addresses inside paths, CRM ids, case numbers,
# tracker keys, Drive ids, Slack channel ids and 24-hex object ids.
#
# This file is an EXAMPLE and is tracked, so do not put real names in it.

# Acme Corporation
# Initech
# Project Codename
